        {
          "id": "81a3ca45-da4b-43da-b381-37641add2cb4",
          "name": "api approvals audit requests actions list",
          "request": {
            "name": "api approvals audit requests actions list",
            "description": {
              "content": "`GET /approvals/audit/requests/<request_id>/actions/` (Notion E5).\n\nCompact per-request action history used by the FE's §1.4 side-by-side\ndisplay: at the Head Decider level the FE renders both the advisor's\noriginal submit value AND the previous Decider's counter (modify)\nvalue side-by-side. Reads `results[0]` for the submit + walks the\nlist for the latest `modify` action.\n\nAuth: standard advisor/decider permission — the FE caller is whoever\nis acting on the bundle, not a compliance-team auditor, so this\nendpoint deliberately does NOT use `CanReadAuditApi`. Authorisation\non the request itself (advisor sees only their own bundles, decider\nsees only assigned ones) is enforced at the queryset level.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "api",
                "approvals",
                "audit",
                "requests",
                ":request_id",
                "actions",
                ""
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<integer>",
                  "key": "request_id",
                  "description": "(Required) "
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{bearerToken}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
